      "message": "Note: My two comments on `ScalePlaneBilinearUp()` also apply to `ScalePlaneBilinearUp_16()`.\n\n---\n\n`ScalePlaneBilinearUp()` has only one caller. It calls `ScalePlaneBilinearUp()` as follows;\n\n```\n  if (filtering \u0026\u0026 dst_height \u003e src_height) {\n    return ScalePlaneBilinearUp(src_width, src_height, dst_width, dst_height,\n                                src_stride, dst_stride, src, dst, filtering);\n  }\n```\n\nThis is why I suggested `assert(dst_height \u003e src_height)` instead of `assert(dst_height \u003e 0)`. \n\nFrom `src_height \u003e 0` and `dst_height \u003e src_height`, it follows that `dst_height \u003e 0`.",
